    "question_text": "Multiply.\n(a) $\\frac38\\times\\frac7{11}$\n(b) $4\\frac27\\times1\\frac38$",
    "solution_text": "(a) $\\frac38\\times\\frac7{11}$\n$=\\frac{3\\times7}{8\\times11}$\n$=\\frac{21}{88}$\n\n(b) $4\\frac27=\\frac{4\\times7+2}{7}=\\frac{30}{7}$ and $1\\frac38=\\frac{1\\times8+3}{8}=\\frac{11}{8}$.\n$\\frac{30}{7}\\times\\frac{11}{8}$\n$=\\frac{330}{56}$\n$=\\frac{165}{28}$\n$=5\\frac{25}{28}$"
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Calculate.\n(a) $\\frac79\\div\\frac4{11}$\n(b) $\\frac58\\div\\frac37\\times\\frac29$",
    "solution_text": "(a) $\\frac79\\div\\frac4{11}$\n$=\\frac79\\times\\frac{11}{4}$\n$=\\frac{77}{36}$\n$=2\\frac5{36}$\n\n(b) Work from left to right.\n$\\frac58\\div\\frac37=\\frac58\\times\\frac73=\\frac{35}{24}$\n$\\frac{35}{24}\\times\\frac29$\n$=\\frac{70}{216}$\n$=\\frac{35}{108}$"
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Find the missing fraction.\n(a) Multiplying a fraction by $\\frac49$ gives $\\frac7{15}$.\n(b) Dividing a fraction by $\\frac7{10}$ gives $\\frac38$.",
    "solution_text": "(a) Undo multiplying by $\\frac49$ by dividing by it.\n$\\frac7{15}\\div\\frac49$\n$=\\frac7{15}\\times\\frac94$\n$=\\frac{63}{60}$\n$=\\frac{21}{20}$\nCheck: $\\frac{21}{20}\\times\\frac49=\\frac7{15}$.\n\n(b) Undo dividing by $\\frac7{10}$ by multiplying by it.\n$\\frac38\\times\\frac7{10}$\n$=\\frac{21}{80}$\nCheck: $\\frac{21}{80}\\div\\frac7{10}=\\frac38$."
  }
]
